From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arkadiusz Hiler <ahiler@codeweavers.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Feb 2023 21:24:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] HACK: kernelbase: Do not flash the winedbg console window.

Depending on what the crashing software does with the handles / own
console we may end up creating a new console window for windbg.

Since Proton defaults to starting windbg in a non-interactive mode
without displaying the crash dialog and redirects the log to unix's
stderr we want to avoid confusing users.

CW-Bug-Id: #21872
(cherry picked from commit ff29c0163d5d990a08e5a3ba9593e5965db6f9d6)

mproton-resolved: kept athei's STARTF_USESTDHANDLES handles, added CREATE_NO_WINDOW
---
 dlls/kernelbase/debug.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
index 0a03bc9a5e6..4247c91ba7e 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
@@ -581,7 +581,7 @@ static BOOL start_debugger( EXCEPTION_POINTERS *epointers, HANDLE event )
     startup.hStdInput = GetStdHandle( STD_INPUT_HANDLE );
     startup.hStdOutput = GetStdHandle( STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE );
     startup.hStdError = GetStdHandle( STD_ERROR_HANDLE );
-    ret = CreateProcessW( NULL, cmdline, NULL, NULL, TRUE, CREATE_UNICODE_ENVIRONMENT, env, NULL, &startup, &info );
+    ret = CreateProcessW( NULL, cmdline, NULL, NULL, TRUE, CREATE_UNICODE_ENVIRONMENT | CREATE_NO_WINDOW, env, NULL, &startup, &info );
     FreeEnvironmentStringsW( env );
 
     if (ret)
